<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēductĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		seduco. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> (Acc. to
			seduco, I.) * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A leading</i> or <i>drawing
			aside</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seductiones testium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Mur. 24, 49</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A misleading</i>, <i>seduction</i>
			(eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Adam confessus est seductionem, non occultavit
					seductricem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 2, 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Luc. 7, §
			218</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cordis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Jer. 23, 26</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iniquitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2
					Thess. 2, 10</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> (Acc. to seduco, II.) <i>A separation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mors est corporis animaeque seductio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 2, 12, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
